baseMap(WittRingMap) -- Returns the underlying RingMap of a WittRingMap
***********************************************************************

  * Function: baseMap (missing documentation)
  * Usage: 
        f = baseMap Wf
  * Inputs:
      * Wf, an instance of the type *note WittRingMap: WittRingMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 

Description
===========

Given a WittRingMap $W(f): W_n(R) \to W_n(S)$ induced by f:R-> S, this returns
the underlying RingMap f: R->S.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : R = (ZZ/5)[x,y];          |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : S = (ZZ/5)[a,b,c,d];      |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(S, R, {a*b, c*d});|
|                               |
|o3 : RingMap S <-- R           |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : Wf = witt(2, f);          |
+-------------------------------+
|i5 : f === baseMap Wf          |
|                               |
|o5 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note baseMap(WittRingMap): baseMap_lpWittRingMap_rp, -- Returns the
    underlying RingMap of a WittRingMap
