explicit(WittIdeal) -- Obtains the explicit version of a WittIdeal.
*******************************************************************

  * Function: explicit (missing documentation)
  * Usage: 
        J := explicit(WI)
  * Inputs:
      * WI, an instance of the type *note WittIdeal: WittIdeal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

If WR is a WittPolynomialRing or WittQuotientRing, and WI is an WittIdeal in
WR, explicit(WI) gives the ideal corresponding to WI in explicit(WR)

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : R := (ZZ/2)[x,y];       |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : w1 := witt{x,y};        |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : w2 := witt{x^2, y^2};   |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : I := wittIdeal(w1, w2)  |
|                             |
|                      2   2  |
|o4 = ideal ({x, y}, {x , y })|
|                             |
|o4 : WittIdeal               |
+-----------------------------+

