truncate(ZZ,WittPolynomialRing) -- Crop Witt ring to the ring of Witt vectors of a given length
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note truncate: (Macaulay2Doc)truncate,
  * Usage: 
        V=truncate(n,W)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * W, an instance of the type *note WittPolynomialRing:
        WittPolynomialRing,,
  * Outputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note WittPolynomialRing:
        WittPolynomialRing,,

Description
===========

This crops W to have length n if n is less than or equal than the length of W.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=ZZ/3[x,y]                      |
|                                      |
|o1 = S                                |
|                                      |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : W=witt(3,S)                      |
|                                      |
|o2 = Witt (S)                         |
|         3                            |
|                                      |
|o2 : WittPolynomialRing               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : truncate(2,W)                    |
|                                      |
|o3 = WittRingMap Witt (S) <-- Witt (S)|
|                     2            3   |
|                                      |
|o3 : WittRingMap                      |
+--------------------------------------+

This should give V a Witt ring with WittLength 2

We get an error if we try to truncate to something longer. For instance,
truncate(4,W) above would return an error.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note truncate(ZZ,WittPolynomialRing):
    truncate_lpZZ_cmWittPolynomialRing_rp, -- Crop Witt ring to the ring of
    Witt vectors of a given length
