      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * W, an instance of the type *note WittQuotientRing: WittQuotientRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note WittQuotientRing: WittQuotientRing,, 

Description
===========

This crops W to have length n if n is less than or equal than the length of W.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = (ZZ/5)[x,y,z] / ideal(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)|
|                                               |
|o1 = S                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : QuotientRing                              |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : W=witt(3,S)                               |
|                                               |
|o2 = Witt (S)                                  |
|         3                                     |
|                                               |
|o2 : WittQuotientRing                          |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : truncate(2,W)                             |
|                                               |
|o3 = WittRingMap Witt (S) <-- Witt (S)         |
|                     2            3            |
|                                               |
|o3 : WittRingMap                               |
+-----------------------------------------------+

This should give V a WittQuotientRing with WittLength 2

We get an error if we try to truncate to something longer. For instance,
truncate(4,W) above would return an error.

