witt(ZZ,ZZ,RingMap) -- The map induced on Witt rings by a RingMap.
******************************************************************

  * Function: witt (missing documentation)
  * Usage: 
        witt(n, m, f)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * Wf, an instance of the type *note WittRingMap: WittRingMap,, 

Description
===========

Given f: R -> S a RingMap between rings  of positive characteristic and an
integer $n \geq 1$, witt(n, f) returns the WittRingMap $W_n(f): W_n(R) \to
W_n(S)$. If two integers $m \geq n \geq 1$ are passed, witt(n, m, f) returns
the WittRingMap given by the composition $W_m(R) \to W_m(S) \to W_n(S)$, where
the last map is truncation.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = (ZZ/5)[x,y];                 |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = (ZZ/5)[a,b,c,d];             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(S, R, {a*b, c*d});       |
|                                      |
|o3 : RingMap S <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : witt(2, 3, f)                    |
|                                      |
|o4 = WittRingMap Witt (S) <-- Witt (R)|
|                     2            3   |
|                                      |
|o4 : WittRingMap                      |
+--------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note witt(ZZ,ZZ,RingMap): witt_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmRingMap_rp, -- The map induced
    on Witt rings by a RingMap.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

