wittLength -- Returns the length of the Witt vectors in a given Witt ring
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        n = wittLength(WR)
  * Inputs:
      * WR, an instance of the type *note WittPolynomialRing:
        WittPolynomialRing,,
      * WR, an instance of the type *note WittQuotientRing: WittQuotientRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

If $WR = W_n(R)$ for some polynomial or quotient ring R, and some integer $n
\geq 1$, wittLength(WR) returns the integer n.

+---------------------+
|i1 : R = GF(9)[x,y]; |
+---------------------+
